  "notes": "Surface derived 2026-07-26 from the CSS Animations Level 2 and CSS Transitions Level 2 Working Drafts (delta specs; resolved via csswg-drafts issue #9010): exactly four items — two attributes (AnimationEvent.animation: CSSAnimation?; TransitionEvent.animation: CSSTransition?) and two dictionary fields (AnimationEventInit.animation, TransitionEventInit.animation, both default null). Documented divergences, preserved rather than smoothed over: (1) Chromium IDL types both attributes/members as the wider Animation? ([RuntimeEnabled=AnimationEventAnimation], stable at trunk) — UA-dispatched values remain CSSAnimation/CSSTransition (WPT-asserted); (2) the transition attribute's spec anchor is the unusually cased #Events-TransitionEvent-animation while the animations spec uses #dom-animationevent-animation; (3) the animations spec's privacy/security anchors are #priv/#sec, the transitions spec's are #privacy/#security; (4) neither spec annotates [SameObject]/[NewObject] — Blink stores and returns the identical object (animation_event.cc/transition_event.cc) and WPT pins identity against getAnimations() for animation events. Null semantics: UA-dispatched events always carry the firing animation (Chromium css_animations.cc dispatch path); null marks script-constructed events (dictionary default null; isTrusted separates authored from native). BCD api/AnimationEvent.json + api/TransitionEvent.json: chrome 151 / edge mirror / firefox 152 / safari 27, each recording mdn_url (MDN attribute page) and spec_url (the level-2 definition; the transition entry confirms the unusually cased anchor); webstatus.dev has no tracked web-feature (zero query hits), so no official Baseline badge is claimed despite all-engines support. MDN has dedicated attribute pages (AnimationEvent.animation, TransitionEvent.animation — value/spec/compat, no Examples section as of 2026-07-26): per the cycle-16 MDN checklist the coverage is not 'full' (examples missing), so this is a Case B full reference, and the integrator may reclassify to a Case A stub if they weigh MDN's coverage as sufficient. MDN pages are linked from the overview's See also. Independent primary-source review of the inventory and prose remains an integrator obligation."
}
